      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "First, you must treat that swollen battery like a live, angry goblin that just found a matchstick in its pocket; if you don't handle it with the caution of a goblin guarding a treasure chest of dynamite, it might just decide to explode in your face.\n\n**Immediate Safety Steps:**\n1.  **Isolate it:** Move the phone to a cool, dry, non-flammable area away from anything flammable, like a pile of old rags or a goblin's favorite kindling. Do not put it in a trash bin; that's like tossing a goblin into a volcano.\n2.  **Don't squeeze:** Never try to crush or puncture the swollen battery. If you do, you're essentially poking a goblin in the eye with a sharp stick, which will just make it angry and release more dangerous gas.\n3.  **No liquids:** Do not spray water or any cleaning solution on it. Water is like a goblin trying to drown a fire; it might put out the visible flames but will just make the situation worse underneath.\n4.  **Ventilation:** Keep the area well-ventilated so any gas the battery is releasing doesn't build up",
